    "res = llm.invoke(\"what is GenAI?\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "b269a6bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "'Let\\'s break down Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI). At its most basic, **GenAI refers to AI models that can create new content - anything from text, images, audio, and code – based on the patterns learned from existing datasets.** Think of it like teaching an AI not just *what* to do, but *how* to think creatively.\\n\\nHere\\'s a more detailed look at the core aspects:\\n\\n**1. How it Works - The Basics**\\n\\n* **Deep Learning:** GenAI systems almost always rely on **deep neural networks**,  a type of AI that has a complex, layered structure.\\n* **Generative Models:** The \"generative\" part means the models *generate* new data. They don\\'t just analyze something – they essentially *make* something new. Popular examples include:\\n    * **ChatGPT:** Creates text based on prompts.\\n    * **Midjourney/DALL-E/Stable Diffusion:** Generates images from textual prompts.\\n    * **LaMDA/Bard:**  Generates conversational answers and text.\\n\\n\\n**2. Types of GenAI & What They Can Generate**\\n\\n* **Text Generation (like ChatGPT, LLaMA):** Writing stories, articles, code, translations, etc.\\n* **Image Generation (like Dall-E, Midjourney, Stable Diffusion):** Creating original images – photorealistic photos, artistic masterpieces, or even stylized variations.\\n* **Voice Synthesis (like Microsoft Aurora, ElevenLabs):** Creating synthetic voices to have chatbots or speech.\\n* **Music Generation (like Riffusion):** Producing music in various styles based on parameters.\\n* **Video Generation (Emerging):**  While more nascent, some models can create short video segments from text prompts or existing footage.\\n\\n**3. Why It Matters**\\n\\n* **Transformation & Content Creation:** GenAI can dramatically speed up the creative process and generate a wider variety of content compared to humans alone. \\n* **Automation:** It can handle repetitive tasks that need creativity, allowing for automation in services across many fields. \\n* **Customization:** It\\'s making personalized experiences possible.\\n\\n\\n**4. Important Note - They are *assistants*, not Replacements** \\n\\n*  It\\'s crucial to remember that these tools aren’t meant to completely replace human work.  They’re best used as *assistants* which increase human productivity and creativity.\\n\\n**5. Key Challenges:**\\n\\n* **Ethical concerns** - Generative AI can be misused for deepfakes, plagiarism, or other harmful purposes\\n* **Bias:**  Training data can contain biases that will impact the model output \\n*   **Lack of true understanding:** They don\\'t truly \"think\" or possess subjective experience – they are highly sophisticated pattern-matching algorithms.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Resources for Further Learning:**\\n\\n*   **OpenAI (ChatGPT)**:  [https://openai.com/](https://openai.com/)\\n*   **Google Arts & Sciences - GenAI**:[https://artsandsciences.withgoogle.com/genai](https://artsandsciences.withgoogle.com/genai)\\n*   **Stanford\\'s GAN Course:** [https://www.cs.stanford.edu/~guttag/course/2019.pdf](https://www.cs.stanford.edu/course/2019.pdf)  (Provides a foundational understanding)\\n\\nDo you want me to:\\n\\n* Explain a specific aspect in more detail (e.g.,  training data)?\\n* Compare GenAI with previous AI types (like image recognition)?\\n* Show you some example GenAI tools (with brief explanations)?'"
      ]
     },
